text:
mia: Heads-up from a quick a11y pass on the new Insights layout. Found four small but sticky issues: focus visuals missing in Firefox, low contrast on tiny hint text under charts, a side-panel that steals focus after collapse, and screen readers not announcing sort/state on the table rows.

rahul: thanks mia. can you paste repro steps + browsers?

mia: repro: mac Firefox 115 + VoiceOver; Windows Firefox + NVDA; also spot-checked Chrome. Steps: 1) open Insights -> hit TAB across main header; Firefox focuses but no visible ring (we removed outline globally); 2) open a chart hover hint (12px) and check contrast with bg — fails 3.2:1; 3) open the Filters panel, collapse it via the toggle, then press tab — focus lands behind the page on an interactive CTA; 4) in the Projects table use keyboard to sort columns, NVDA doesn't say whether it's ascending/descending.

tess: i can reproduce the filter collapse trap. looks like when we animate height to 0 we leave the panel in DOM and the focus-lock lib thinks it's still active. adding inert to the main content on open would help. also, the collapse toggle isn't aria-expanded on the button.

noah: product-wise we want the animation, but accessibility shouldn't suffer. can we have both? maybe keep visual collapse with CSS transitions but ensure we toggle aria-hidden/inert after animation finishes.

rahul: agree. plan: (A) remove the global outline:none and adopt :focus-visible with a strong token; (B) bump hint text weight or use a semi-bold variant for chart captions and add a 1px darken stroke if needed; (C) update the panel collapse flow to set aria-hidden/inert after transitionend and ensure the toggle button has aria-expanded toggled immediately for SRs. for the table: add aria-sort on th and use aria-live on a dedicated sr-only region to announce "Sorted by X, descending" after change.

a11y-bot: automated check (axe-core 4.x): findings -> color-contrast x2 (chart hint + footer legal), focus-outline-none x1, focus-trap x1, table-headers-aria x1. recommendations: use dedicated live region, ensure aria-expanded on toggles, and avoid removing focus indicators globally.

mia: sample code for toggle button: 
```html
<button id="filters-toggle" aria-expanded="false">Filters</button>
<div id="filters-panel" aria-hidden="true">...controls...</div>
```
and JS: 
```js
const btn = document.getElementById('filters-toggle');
const panel = document.getElementById('filters-panel');
btn.addEventListener('click', () => {
  const open = btn.getAttribute('aria-expanded') === 'true';
  btn.setAttribute('aria-expanded', String(!open));
  if (!open) {
    panel.style.height = 'auto';
    panel.setAttribute('aria-hidden', 'false');
    // after transition
    panel.addEventListener('transitionend', () => panel.removeAttribute('inert'));
  } else {
    panel.style.height = '0px';
    panel.setAttribute('aria-hidden', 'true');
    panel.setAttribute('inert', '');
  }
});
```

rahul: thanks, will PR these fixes: focus-visible token, chart hint color token swap, panel inert/timing fix, aria-sort on table headers + small live-region message. will include repro steps and axe before+after.

tess: i'll run NVDA/VoiceOver passes on the deploy preview and flag any remaining announces. also adding an automated keyboard-tab test to CI that tabs across header and asserts focus-visible present.

noah: prioritize the panel trap and focus-visible for the next patch. the chart hint contrast can follow in the next sprint if we need design sign-off.

mia: sounds good. adding tasks to the design board and noting acceptance criteria: visible focus indicator, no focus escape on panel collapse, aria-sort announced on change, and chart-hint meets 4.5:1 or uses a stronger token. :sparkles:
